Rosemary is a hybrid compatibility layer and high-level emulator designed for
running macOS applications across operating systems and CPU architectures. To
elaborate on CPU emulation, it utilizes Microlift to translate arm64 calls to
x86 equivalents and vice versa on the fly with Cranelift.

As Rosemary is a new project that primarily targets Linux and macOS over FreeBSD
(despite official support), the current capabilities are not extensive, and you
may run into issues.
